# PowerZebra Benchmark — environment variables
#
# 1. Copy this file:      cp .env.benchmark.example .env.benchmark
#    (Windows PowerShell: Copy-Item .env.benchmark.example .env.benchmark)
# 2. Fill in the values below (ask ZAN for the PowerZebra URL + API key).
# 3. Run:  npm run benchmark:cuda   then   npm run benchmark:zan
#
# This file (.env.benchmark) is gitignored — it is safe to put real API keys
# in it. Never commit real keys to .env.benchmark.example.
#
# Full instructions: docs/BENCHMARK_RUNBOOK.md

# ── (A) CUDA baseline — current Theta EdgeCloud SP1 prover ─────────────────
# The live SP1 prover host URL (same one used in production, see env.example
# SP1_PROVER_URL). No trailing slash.
BENCHMARK_CUDA_URL=
# Leave blank unless the CUDA endpoint requires an API key.
BENCHMARK_CUDA_API_KEY=
# Optional: $/GPU-hour, used to compute a $/proof estimate in the report.
BENCHMARK_CUDA_COST_PER_HOUR=2.50

# ── (B) ZAN PowerZebra candidate — fill in once ZAN provisions access ──────
# ZAN will give you a URL like https://<something>.zan.top or an IP:port.
BENCHMARK_ZAN_URL=
# The API key ZAN gives you (sent as the "x-api-key" header).
BENCHMARK_ZAN_API_KEY=
# Optional: $/GPU-hour ZAN quotes you, for the $/proof comparison.
BENCHMARK_ZAN_COST_PER_HOUR=
